@startuml dispatch
'
' Engineered by  Christian Schnapka
'                Embedded Principal+ Engineer
'                Macstab GmbH · Hamburg, Germany
'                https://macstab.com
'
' Dispatch of one interposed call with a matching rule, as libchaos-io
' and libchaos-net do it (one rule per call). Shows the lazy symbol
' table, the re-entrancy guard, the throttled rule-file check, rule
' selection, the firing decision, the raw-syscall sleep, the real call
' and the post-call mutation.
'
' Reference: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md "Request flow", docs/DSL.md §8
'            src/wrappers/chaos_io_rw.c, src/effects/chaos_io_actions.c
'
title Full Dispatcher Flow — Interposed Symbol with Matched Rule

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 4
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor                 #2C3E50
  LifeLineBorderColor        #2C3E50
  LifeLineBackgroundColor    #ECF0F1
  ParticipantBorderColor     #2C3E50
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantFontStyle       bold
  GroupBackgroundColor       #FDFEFE
  GroupBorderColor           #95A5A6
}
hide footbox

participant "Application"           as App
participant "Wrapper"               as Wrap
participant "TLS Guard"             as Guard
participant "Config Engine"         as Config
participant "Selector\nResolver"    as Sel
participant "Effect Engine"         as FX
participant "Real function\n(RTLD_NEXT)" as Real

App -> Wrap : symbol(args…)
Wrap -> Wrap : ensure_symbols()\n(chaos_once: one acquire load once done)
note right of Wrap
  First call: dlsym(RTLD_NEXT) for the whole
  table. A call re-entering from inside dlsym
  finds its pointer NULL and issues the raw
  system call (or fails with ENOSYS).
end note
Wrap -> Guard : in_internal()?
note right of Guard
  __thread int flag (saved and restored),
  set only while the library runs its own
  code: the real call, the rule-file read,
  the /proc/self/fd readlink.
end note

alt Guard set (call made from this library's own code)
  Wrap -> Real : direct call, no injection
  Real --> Wrap : result
  Wrap --> App : result
else Guard clear (normal path)

  Wrap -> Config : prepare()
  note right of Config
    skip unless >= 1 ms since the last look
    (vDSO CLOCK_MONOTONIC; never skipped while
     the stamp is UNKNOWN or RELOADING)
    stat(rule file) → change stamp
    if changed or load provisional:
      CAS(stamp, cached, RELOADING)
      winner: read, fstat-check, parse,
              publish inactive snapshot
      loser:  use the active snapshot now
    errno restored
  end note
  Config --> Wrap : any rule loaded?

  Wrap -> Sel : resolve_selector(args…)
  note right of Sel
    io:  fd → fd cache → /proc/self/fd path
         (fd 0-2 and excluded paths never match)
    net: socket → endpoint (sockaddr or
         getsockname/getpeername); net
         resolves it before prepare()
  end note
  Sel --> Wrap : selector

  Wrap -> Config : select_rule(op, selector)
  note right of Config
    most specific rule for the operation;
    seqlock: a copy made while a reload
    rewrote the snapshot is discarded
  end note
  Config --> Wrap : rule copy (or none)

  alt No rule matched
    Wrap -> Real : real_function(args…)
    Real --> Wrap : result
    Wrap --> App : result
  else Rule matched
    Wrap -> FX : should_trigger(rule)
    note right of FX
      @from/@until window, @size gate,
      probability (skipped for LATENCY):
        sample < p · 2^32
        (sample: per-thread xorshift64* u32)
      @first claim (CAS), hit counted
    end note

    alt ERRNO fired (pre-call)
      FX --> Wrap : errno = rule.errnum
      Wrap --> App : -1
    else LATENCY, TORN, CORRUPT, or not fired
      opt LATENCY fired
        FX -> FX : chaos_sleep_ms()\nraw clock_nanosleep(CLOCK_MONOTONIC),\nEINTR restarted with the remainder, errno kept
      end
      Wrap -> Real : real_function(args…) under the guard\n(TORN fired: count shortened to [1, count-1])
      Real --> Wrap : result
      opt CORRUPT rule and result > 0 (decided after the call)
        Wrap -> FX : should_trigger(rule) → flip one bit\nof the bytes returned
      end
      Wrap --> App : result (possibly mutated)
    end
  end
end

note across
  libchaos-net also selects one rule per call and adds TIMEOUT, RESET, TRICKLE and DUP
  (docs/NETWORK.md). libchaos-dns, -time, -memory and -process select one rule per effect:
  LATENCY, then ERRNO / EAI_* / FAIL_AFTER, then the real call, then post-call effects
  (time: OFFSET, REGRESS; dns: FILTER_FAMILY, SHUFFLE, LIMIT), each with its own lookup
  and firing decision. libchaos-time sleeps through the real usleep/nanosleep under its
  guard; every other library sleeps with chaos_sleep_ms().
end note

@enduml
